{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "7f6b9f2e-4a1c-4e2b-9a63-0d3c5a1b8e42",
    "name": "ApexTick Booking API",
    "description": "Full surface of the ApexTick booking-service (Spring Boot, port **8081**).\n\n**Quick start**\n1. Select the *ApexTick Local* environment, and set `username` and `password` to your account.\n2. `01 · Auth → Get token` - stores `{{accessToken}}`; every request inherits it as Bearer auth.\n3. `02 · Catalog → Event detail` then `Seats for event` - saves `eventId`, `seatId1`, `seatId2`.\n4. `03 · Holds → Hold seats` → `04 · Orders → Create order` → `Pay (mock card)`.\n5. `05 · Tickets → Tickets for order` → `Ticket PDF` (use *Send and Download*), then `08 · Gate → Scan ticket`.\n\n**Notes**\n- The token comes from the confidential `apextick-loadtest` client; `clientSecret` is `LOADTEST_CLIENT_SECRET` from `.env`.\n- Errors are RFC-7807 `application/problem+json`, with a machine-readable `code`.\n- If port 8081 is taken, run booking-service on another port and change `baseUrl`.\n- Admin needs the `admin` realm role, and Gate the `admin` or `scanner` role: `scripts/grant-role.sh admin|scanner <user>`, then a new token.\n- Realtime seat updates are STOMP over `/api/ws`, outside Postman's HTTP scope.\n- The WSO2 gateway fronts this same API in production; the collection talks to the service directly.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{accessToken}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "01 · Auth",
      "description": "Run **Get token** first. It logs in to Keycloak with the resource-owner-password (direct) grant and stores the JWT in `{{accessToken}}`, which every other request inherits as a Bearer token. Tokens are short-lived (~5 min) - when anything starts returning 401, just re-run this.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Get token (Keycloak password grant)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"Token issued\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "if (json.access_token) {",
                  "    pm.environment.set(\"accessToken\", json.access_token);",
                  "    console.log(\"accessToken saved, expires in \" + json.expires_in + \"s\");",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{keycloakUrl}}/realms/{{realm}}/protocol/openid-connect/token",
              "host": [
                "{{keycloakUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "realms",
                "{{realm}}",
                "protocol",
                "openid-connect",
                "token"
              ]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "urlencoded",
              "urlencoded": [
                {
                  "key": "grant_type",
                  "value": "password",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "key": "client_id",
                  "value": "{{clientId}}",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "key": "client_secret",
                  "value": "{{clientSecret}}",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "key": "username",
                  "value": "{{username}}",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "key": "password",
                  "value": "{{password}}",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "key": "scope",
                  "value": "openid profile email",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Password grant on the confidential `apextick-loadtest` client: the browser's public client, `apextick-web`, takes authorization code + PKCE only and refuses this grant. `clientSecret` is `LOADTEST_CLIENT_SECRET` from `.env` (`dev-loadtest-secret` locally), and `username`/`password` are your own account's; a demo deployment prints its shared account on the sign-in page. The test script saves `access_token`."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "My profile - GET /api/me",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/me",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "me"
              ]
            },
            "description": "The authenticated user's profile and realm roles, resolved from the JWT. Good smoke test that the token works."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
